<title>CANADA: Air Canada, Canadian get new routes.</title>
<headline>Air Canada, Canadian get new routes.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Transport Minister David Anderson, together with Foreign Affairs Minister Lloyd Axworthy said they had chosen Canadian Airlines Corp unit Canadian Airlines International to serve Belize, Costa Rica, El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras, Nicaragua and Panama.</p>
<p>Air Canada was chosen to serve Denmark, Norway and Sweden.</p>
<p>&quot;With these designations each carrier will have the opportunity to introduce service in a region that it has identified as a priority,&quot; Anderson said in a statement issued on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
